findings.problem:
There is no first-audio deadline and no stall watchdog, so the tutor can stay 'speaking' forever:
(a) if the caller never calls feed.end()/abort() (LLM stream error, useChat stop, unmount), `drive` waits forever, closeSent/finalReceived never happen, and the fallback's queue never ends either;
(b) iOS AudioContext state 'interrupted' (after a call, Siri, or switching apps) isn't checked: currentTime freezes, so `t >= lastEnd` is never true;
(c) if the ElevenLabs server stalls, it only closes after inactivity_timeout=60 s.
While stuck, converse.speaking() is true, so 'yes'/'ok' are dropped and echo filtering keeps running.
